# Line endings, pinned for every platform.
#
# The package is developed on Windows and macOS. Without this file the two checkouts disagree:
# five sources were committed with CRLF, the rest with LF, and a machine whose `core.autocrlf` is
# `true` rewrites every LF file on checkout — so the same commit produces two different working
# trees, `git status` reports files nobody touched, and a diff shows whole files as changed.
#
# Normalising is safe here because the built artifact does not depend on source line endings:
# `node build.mjs` produces byte-identical `client.js` from an all-CRLF tree and an all-LF tree
# (verified 2026-11-04, sha256:8199a25b5bbc5d94 both ways). See DEFECTS.md 3.3, which recorded the
# opposite expectation before it was measured.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
